        "original_id": "5dc1dd53-28ae-560b-8482-a68fd92408e9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Interbol\n- Organizations: Russian Space Agency, Space Research Institute of the Russian Academy of Sciences\n- Places: tail of the magnetosphere, Van Allen radiation belt\n- Concepts: plasma, ions, electrons, electric fields, electric currents, magnetic fields\n\nFacts:\n- Interbol is an international space project led by the Russian Space Agency and the Space Research Institute of the Russian Academy of Sciences.\n- Interbol aims to study correlations in the tail of the magnetosphere and in the Van Allen radiation belt.\n- Plasma can be considered a gaseous mixture of negatively charged electrons and highly charged positive ions.\n- True plasma production results from the distinct separation of ions and electrons.\n- The separation of ions and electrons produces an electric field.\n- The electric field produces electric currents and magnetic fields.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e26bf770-8b6e-5cf9-af5a-e618f0d96026",
        "text": "Interbol is an international space project under the leadership of the Russian Space Agency and the Space Research Institute of the Russian Academy of Sciences, the goal being to study the correlations between which items can simply be considered as a gaseous mixture of negatively charged electrons and highly charged positive ions; true plasma production, however, is from the distinct separation of these ions and electrons that produces an electric field, which in turn, produces electric currents and magnetic fields, in the tail of the magnetosphere and in the Van Allen radiation belt.",
